Original commit body from 331f6333399ea8efdc7ccac884270eea4fae3606:

Every other taint test hands verify-claims a hand-written behavior map via
--input, so the analyzers never run. verify_taint_claim is fed hand-built
TaintFlowFinding objects, and the single test that puts real source on disk
asserts `rc in (0, 1)` -- a branch-touch, not a behaviour. Nothing in the
suite would have failed if the pipeline stopped reporting an entire class of
real flows, which is how ten ADR-0017 capabilities came to sit inert while
each was closed done on 100% coverage.

test_taint_recall_corpus.py generates Python and Go repos into tmp_path and
runs analysis -> propagation -> claim verification, asserting which flows
come out.

Vacuity is structurally impossible rather than guarded against. A corpus of
"must NOT be reported" assertions passes trivially when the pipeline reports
nothing (L17) -- the exact failure mode here, since a broken propagator makes
every precision assertion greener. Each language arm therefore puts the
must-find and must-not-find shapes in ONE repo and asserts the whole finding
set at once, so a pipeline emitting nothing fails the must-find half.

Proven by mutation in both propagators: silencing propagate_taint_structural
turns the Go arm red, silencing propagate_taint_ddg turns the Python arm red.
That they fail different tests is itself the finding -- cli.py routes Python
through the DDG pass and everything else through the structural pass, so a
Python-only regression test could never have covered Go's path.

The first positive control FAILED and shaped the corpus (L9): a source and a
sink under a common caller report nothing, because propagation seeds at the
source's caller and walks forward only. reverse_adj is built and never read.
Recorded as xfail(strict=True) so it XPASSes when source-side propagation
lands (L19); the imperative form could never XPASS and would silently
disable the signal.

Catalog entries are chosen, not assumed: every source and sink is
module-qualified and verified absent from its language's ambiguous_names
(asyncio.start_server -> os.mkdir; net/http.ListenAndServe -> os.WriteFile).
INV-karud's own first control returned a clean zero for exactly that reason.

Generated into tmp_path deliberately -- a fixture corpus analyzed in place
measures the pipeline's test-path heuristics rather than the producer
(L20/L21), and verify-claims now excludes test-sourced flows by default, so
a corpus under a directory named fixtures would be excluded from its own
verdicts.

Also repairs a CHANGELOG bullet whose header was lost in an earlier edit,
leaving the _sink_module_compatible retirement entry starting mid-sentence.

